# One node address per line. Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
# Everything after the address on a line is ignored too, so you can annotate.
#
# These are the addresses the container uses for both:
#   - mpirun -H          (peer-to-peer ssh, port 7900 inside the container)
#   - NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME (the bootstrap/TCP interface on each node)
# so they must be the addresses bound to NETWORK_IF in set_env.sh, and they must
# be reachable from each other.
#
# Order matters for split_ip.sh: it takes nodes in file order, and for GB racks
# it expects one rack's nodes to be contiguous (18 per rack).
#
# node01  # optional comment
# node02
# node03
